Z||000000||Haze_Performance||06-20-2000||04:16 AM||||I would like a set of 16" chrome 2000 5-star wheels off a Grand Am. Someone must find out if you can swap the rotors/hubs into a Fiero. (Its a diffrent lug patern 112mm) I talked to a a few GM dealers, but they were no help.How can we find out if we can do it??It would be a perfect swap, you would get large 16" wheels,larger & vented rotors + Ive even seen crossdrilled rotors on a 2000 G/A. How cool would that be? <P><BR>Now im drooling  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  <P>||||reg||4
Z||000001||Oreif||06-20-2000||10:27 AM||||Sorry Haze but in order to swap the back hubs to the 112mm you would need custom axle's The 2000 GA use 28mm axle's the fiero use 22mm. For the front there isn't a rotor that has a 112mm pattern and has bearings and studs. I have been looking at many brake upgrades for the past 2 weeks. So far the only vented rotor that will fit the front of a fiero(84-87) is one from a 77-79 chevy monza. But this changes your bolt pattern to a standard size and nobody makes a FWD wheel for the bolt pattern. <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-20-2000).]||||reg||9
